NOTES = {
6: 'The armored regiment split into separate battalions in July 1944. The later 1st and 2d Battalion lineages both descend through companies of the 6th Armored Infantry Battalion; the 4th descends through the 11th. These are lineage rows, not claims that modern battalion headquarters existed in 1944. The August 1921 reassignment is known only to the month.',
10: 'The February 1919 release is known only to the month. Headquarters later activated under TRADOC are training organizations, not division assignments.',
13: 'The February 1959 reassignment is known only to the month, so that month is marked uncertain. Early regimental assignments are recorded in the 1st Battalion lineage; its separate company inactivation in 1929 is not applied to the entire regiment.',
15: 'The Philippine Division assignment applied to the regiment in 1922, but after April 1923 only the old 1st Battalion retained it. That battalion was inactivated in 1929 and released in 1931. The common row therefore marks 1923-1940 as mixed/unverified instead of assigning the entire China-based regiment to the Philippine Division.',
19: 'The 2d Battle Group received its own assignment in 1957, before the parent regiment was reorganized in 1958. The overlap is intentional.',
21: 'The Hawaiian Division was reorganized as the 24th Infantry Division in 1941. Formal division assignments are distinguished from brigade attachments in Vietnam.',
25: 'The 25th Infantry Regiment is a different organization from the 25th Infantry Division. Its 93d Division bar begins with documented overseas service in January 1944, not a claimed initial assignment date. The exact 1957 inactivation date is unverified, so the whole year is marked uncertain. No later battalion reactivation is established here.',
28: 'The 2d Battle Group moved to the 1st Infantry Division in February 1957, before the parent regiment completed its reorganization in August. The overlap is intentional.',
29: 'The 1st Battalion lineage records a second 4th Division assignment, June 1940-October 1941, absent from the older regimental certificate. The newer lineage is used here.',
}
